    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "To supervise is to stand FOR others:",
          "kusimama + -i- = kusimamia. This is the",
          "applicative: -i-/-e- before the final -a.",
          "",
          "   kuleta    to bring",
          "   kuletea   to bring TO someone",
          "",
          "   kupika    to cook",
          "   kupikia   to cook FOR someone",
          "",
          "   Muuguzi ananiletea dawa.",
          "   The nurse brings me medicine.",
          "",
          "   Mama anawapikia watoto.",
          "   Mother cooks for the children.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Kuletea. Muuguzi ananiletea dawa. Mama anawapikia watoto."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "The vowel obeys harmony: roots with",
          "e or o take -e-, the rest take -i-:",
          "",
          "   kusoma  -> kusomea   study for/at",
          "   kuandika -> kuandikia write to",
          "",
          "   Ninakuandikia barua.",
          "   I am writing you a letter.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "Five beads so far: -w-, -ik-, -an-,",
          "ji- and now -i-; the causative -ish-",
          "closes this tier. Every verb in this",
          "pack is these beads at work — read the",
          "bead, know the verb."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Kusomea. Ninakuandikia barua."
        }
      }
    ]
